{"author":{"id":"7c5527b9befade3b1be0c1d677ac996815288d8332f34269730a5b81425ee5be"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1791208919,"nonce":"SC2GBnHe2aWAf6/mA4Vk/LjyRI8=","metadata":{"github-url":"https://github.com/EPFL-ENAC/vps-mitsi/issues/41","origin":"github","sync:github.com/epfl-enac/vps-mitsi:id":"I_kwDOULtcMc8AAAABVItq2g","sync:github.com/epfl-enac/vps-mitsi:labels":"","sync:github.com/epfl-enac/vps-mitsi:number":"41","sync:github.com/epfl-enac/vps-mitsi:status":"open","sync:github.com/epfl-enac/vps-mitsi:text":"77af01c66fc27a6a4891956940d16cfaf74563d9666b2f1249a8c8a88393c0b8","sync:github.com/epfl-enac/vps-mitsi:title":"[REFACTOR](Data model) Remove underlying services and derived totals from the saved format (needs schema migration)","sync:github.com/epfl-enac/vps-mitsi:url":"https://github.com/EPFL-ENAC/vps-mitsi/issues/41"},"title":"[REFACTOR](Data model) Remove underlying services and derived totals from the saved format (needs schema migration)","message":"**Is your feature request related to a problem? Please describe.**\nThe saved assessment format (`MitsiStateSchema` in `frontend/src/models/schema.ts`, `MITSI_SCHEMA_VERSION = 4`) stores data it shouldn't.\n\n1. **Underlying services, a feature excluded from v1, is wired throughout.** The lead decision recorded in `ResultsPage.vue` keeps it out of v1, yet:\n   - the schema defines `UnderlyingServiceSchema` and its draft variant, and `includeUnderlyingServices` and `underlyingServices` are saved in every draft and export;\n   - the store holds both refs and `totalUnderlying`, adds it into `totalLifespan`, and handles it in `reset`, `buildState` and `applyState`;\n   - `TotalSplitPieChart.vue` takes an `underlying` prop and falls back to the hard-coded label `'Underlying services'`;\n   - `ResultsPage.vue` carries v2 comment blocks describing how to switch it on.\n2. **`memoryTotalGb` and `storageTotal` are saved but always recalculated.** `schema.ts` marks both as \"computed in store (quantity × size); not authoritative in exported JSON\". The inventory table always recalculates them, so a saved value can disagree with quantity × size.\n3. **Those two totals are also displayed with the wrong formatter.** `HardwareInventoryTable.vue` renders them with `formatKg`, so 64 GB shows as `64.00`.\n\n**Describe the solution you'd like**\n**Prerequisite (blocking):** removing fields means bumping `MITSI_SCHEMA_VERSION` to 5. Today `parseState` (`stores/mitsi.ts`) rejects any other version:\n- a v4 draft in localStorage silently loads as empty, and the next Save overwrites it;\n- v4 export files are rejected with a generic \"import failed\".\n\nSo a migration path has to exist first. Following \"refactor first, then change behaviour\":\n- [ ] Refactor, no behaviour change: move parsing, serializing and version handling out of the store into a small, pure, tested module.\n- [ ] Behaviour: add a v4 → v5 migration (drop the fields below) and a visible error for unknown versions, both for localStorage drafts and for imported files. Related: #33.\n\nThen:\n- [ ] Delete the underlying-services schema, draft schema and type; the store refs, `totalUnderlying` and their place in `totalLifespan`, `reset`, `buildState` and `applyState`; the chart's `underlying` prop and its hard-coded label; and the v2 comments in `ResultsPage.vue`. Bring it back when v2 is specified.\n- [ ] Remove `memoryTotalGb` and `storageTotal` from `HardwareItemSchema`. Keep them as display-only derived columns.\n- [ ] Format the derived memory and storage totals as GB, not with `formatKg`, and add a regression test.\n- [ ] Update `store.test.mjs` and `schema.test.mjs` with a v4 fixture that migrates to v5.\n\n**Describe alternatives you've considered**\nKeep the fields \"for v2\". That keeps every v1 user's data carrying unused state, keeps a total that can silently include a hidden contribution, and means the v2 design is already fixed before anyone has specified it.\n\n**Additional context**\nRaised in an architecture review of `dev` at `b35fc8c` (section 5). The migration prerequisite is the larger saving/loading issue from that review (section 1), which isn't tracked separately yet.","files":null}]}